{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested on exact head 8d30745d1643c7323191420c9dfc789ee7930204 against fresh request e578bc01 and predecessor decision 8f7d36fd.\n\nThe intended behavior is otherwise present and coherent: retired bases still refuse; merely stale bases are stamped; stale unclaimed reassignment retains the zero-promise and zero-completion guards; workroom-fold@17 is the appropriate cache boundary; all fourteen MCP tools retain withSelection; the eleven docs and surfaces agree. The exact branch tip matches origin. Targeted go test for internal/app, internal/workroom, cmd/gs, and cmd/gitseq-mcp passed, and go vet for those packages passed.\n\nBlocking security defect: the reserved stale_bases testimony is protected only at the friendly client surface. internal/app/admission.go:103-108 rejects it before signing, but the authoritative post-dedup path at lines 260-278 decodes an already-signed payload and calls admitState directly. refuseReservedFields at lines 112-140 explicitly exempts stale_bases unconditionally. refuseDeadBases at lines 187-205 overwrites a cloned body only when a stale basis exists, and admitApplication discards the returned clone. Consequently a hand-crafted signed state on live ground can carry arbitrary body.stale_bases and pass authoritative sequencing; on stale ground an incorrect signed note is not compared with the canonical note. This contradicts the documented claim that stale_bases is boundary-owned testimony and that an admission-skipping writer cannot obtain force.\n\nArchitecture: layers 5 and 7 are affected. The intended layer-5 admission/fold contract and layer-7 CLI/MCP/docs changes are correctly described, but the layer-5 authoritative contract is not enforced for untrusted signed input, so the exact head cannot be approved. Layers 1-4 remain unchanged.\n\nSecurity: actor authority and retired-basis refusal remain intact, but an actor can forge the provenance evidence attributed to the admission boundary. That is an unresolved trust-boundary defect even though the field currently grants no authority.\n\nSimplification: use one pure canonical stale-note computation in both phases. Before signing, add the exact note (or omit the field when no stale basis exists); at sequencing, require the signed field to equal that exact result, including requiring absence on fresh ground. Add mutation-sensitive tests that submit a signed application past client preflight with a forged note on fresh ground and a mismatched note on stale ground, proving authoritative refusal. No new flag or schema is needed.\n\nDo not merge this head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c3c9aa5f1b9f3530e9335fff6b9852d21948c7f8","head":"8d30745d1643c7323191420c9dfc789ee7930204","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2685a201f75a3fbd58b7f71d323ed51836450c67\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c7a7ed39b891e30759350ecc5de9c2595d196fe5","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}